OUTPUT
Reply with a single JSON object and nothing else. Write the rationales FIRST —
one non-empty rationale per dimension — then the scores, so each score follows
from reasoning you have already committed to and stays independently auditable:

{
  "rationales": {
    "factual_correctness": "<why this score was assigned>",
    "completeness": "<why this score was assigned>",
    "format_adherence": "<why this score was assigned>",
    "sql_plausibility": "<why this score was assigned>"
  },
  "factual_correctness": <integer 1-5>,
  "completeness": <integer 1-5>,
  "format_adherence": <integer 1-5>,
  "sql_plausibility": <integer 1-5>
}

Every score must be an integer from 1 to 5 inclusive. Do not emit any other key.
Do not wrap the JSON in code fences.
